.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-FOLLOW 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-follow
.Nd follow every kldload log at once, each line tagged with where it came from
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
follows, in one stream, every log that kldload writes while a machine is
being installed, first-booted and built on: the automatic deployment,
the installer, first boot, the Kubernetes bootstrap and its joins, the
klab driver and each of its machines' serial consoles, and every job the
web console starts \(em golden builds, clones, Ansible runs, Helm
installs.
.Pp
Each line is prefixed with a tag \(em
.Ql deploy ,
.Ql install ,
.Ql firstbt ,
.Ql k8s-bs ,
.Ql klab ,
.Ql console ,
.Ql ansible ,
and so on \(em so interleaved streams can be told apart, coloured on a
terminal.
It starts with the last 30 lines of each log.
.Pp
A log that appears while it runs is picked up within two seconds;
a log that does not exist yet is waited for.
Ctrl-C ends it.
.Pp
Run it as root to see the logs under
.Pa /root/klab .
In the embedded terminal of the web console, F3 opens it.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/log/kldload/*.log
The installer's, first boot's, the deployment's, and every web console
job's logs.
.It Pa /var/log/klab/*.log
klab machines' serial consoles.
.It Pa /root/klab/*.log
The klab driver.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1n -compact
.It 0
Ended with Ctrl-C, or
.Fl -help .
.It 2
An argument was given.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Printed on a kldload desktop on 2026-09-30, stopped after six seconds:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# timeout 6 kldload-follow
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
 kldload-follow — unified live tail (Ctrl-C to exit)
 Streams: autodeploy / klab driver / firstboot / kube-bootstrap
          + every VM console under /var/log/klab/
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

── /var/log/kldload/autodeploy.log ──
deploy  | [klab]     ZFS binary:     MISSING
deploy  | [klab]     ZFS module:     loaded
\&...
.Ed
.Pp
The lines themselves carry the logs' own colour codes, left out here.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr journalctl 1 ,
.Xr tail 1 ,
.Xr klab 8 ,
.Xr kldload-component 8 ,
.Xr kube-cluster 8
.Sh HISTORY
It replaced a follower of the ZFS test lab's logs alone.
.Pp
On 2026-09-30, writing this page:
.Fl -help
started following, and never returned.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
The systemd journal is not followed; a unit that logs only there is seen
with
.Xr journalctl 1 .
